## Live Query Strategy Decision Matrix

### Choose Strategy Based on Dataset Size and Use Case:

**Traditional Live Query** (`useLiveEntity`)
- **Best for**: Small datasets (<100 records), complex client operations
- **Use when**: Rich relationship data needed, complex computations, dashboard with heavy processing
- **Example**: Reference data, user lists, project dropdowns

**Incremental Live Query** (`useLiveEntityIncremental`) 
- **Best for**: Medium datasets (100-1000 records), balanced performance
- **Use when**: Main data tables with complex relationships, moderate real-time needs
- **Example**: Standard task lists, data tables with JOINs

**Live Changes API** (`useLiveChanges`)
- **Best for**: Large datasets (1000+ records), maximum efficiency
- **Use when**: High-frequency updates, bandwidth constraints, simple CRUD operations
- **Example**: Large task lists (5000+ records), real-time collaboration

## Atoms vs Direct Database Queries

### Use Atoms When:
- Real-time collaboration (multiple users editing)
- Frequent updates (CRUD operations)
- Component reactivity (UI needs to react to changes)
- Shared state (multiple components need same data)
- Optimistic updates (immediate UI feedback)

### Query Database Directly When:
- Analytics & reporting (complex aggregations)
- One-time data fetches (modals, forms)
- Large data exports (streaming required)
- Search operations (full-text, complex filters)
- Dashboard metrics (heavy computations)

## Performance Guidelines

### Database Optimization
- Use single query updates (avoid SELECT then UPDATE)
- Implement batch operations for bulk changes
- Leverage database engines for complex aggregations
- Use streaming for large exports

### Application Optimization
- Choose appropriate live query strategy for dataset size
- Use atoms for shared, frequently-updated state
- Use direct queries for one-time operations
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Monitor performance metrics

## Code Patterns

### Domain Service Pattern
```typescript
// Follow pattern in apps/web/src/domain/task.ts
export class TaskService extends BaseService<Task> {
  async createTask(data: CreateTaskData): Promise<Task> {
    // Business logic + automatic sync tracking
  }
}
```

### Atomic State Pattern
```typescript
// Follow pattern in apps/web/src/db/atoms/entities/taskAtoms.ts
const allTasksDataAtom = atom<Task[]>([]);
const taskStatsAtom = atom((get) => {
  const tasks = get(allTasksDataAtom);
  return calculateTaskStats(tasks);
});
```

### Live Query Bridge Pattern
```typescript
// Use atomic bridges for optimal performance
const { performance } = useAtomicLiveChanges(); // For large datasets
const { atoms } = useAtomicLiveQuery(); // For medium datasets
```

